NUM-45: set the concentration of a dry node with no inflow to zero

During a step Node[].newQual[] accumulates the node's mass inflow rate,
which findNodeQual() divides by the inflow. When the inflow is at or below
ZERO and the node is dry, 5.2.4 set the concentration to 0; 5.3.0 lost that
branch (fork commit 5b87a2b5), so the node kept the accumulated load rate
(MASS-type and API loads, sub-ZERO link loads) and reported it as mg/L.
Restore the else branch. Wet nodes and nodes with inflow are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-45_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
index 1cf5ae1..ea19995 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
@@ -265,6 +265,8 @@ void findNodeQual(int j)
                 Node[j].newQual[p] = 0.0;
             else if (Node[j].newDepth > ZeroDepth)
                 Node[j].newQual[p] = Node[j].oldQual[p];
+            else
+                Node[j].newQual[p] = 0.0;
         }
     }
 }
